With that change in place, any unmanaged layer (including the select overlay) will respect its own `zIndex` property instead of always floating above everything else. You can now do, for example:

```js
select.getOverlay().setZIndex(100);  // above most stuff
// or
select.getOverlay().setZIndex(-1);   // underneath custom hover-dots
```

to control the stacking order as you expect.
